<title>VIETNAM: Vietnam targets tea production leap in 1997.</title>
<headline>Vietnam targets tea production leap in 1997.</headline>
<dateline>HANOI 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Vietnam is planning to produce 45,000 tonnes of tea this year, a rise of almost 30 percent from 35,000 tonnes in 1996, official media reports said on Monday.</p>
<p>Vietnam Tea Corporation, the industry's state-owned monopoly, is aiming to increase its exports of tea to between 20,000 and 22,000 tonnes from last year's 16,000 tonnes, which brought earnings of $25 million.</p>
<p>No figures for production and export in 1995 were given, though the daily Vietnam News said it had been &quot;a year of heavy losses&quot;.</p>
</text>
